.TH KAGI-BENCH 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "Developer Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-bench \- benchmark Kagi's erasure coding and reconstruction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-bench
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates reproducible in-memory payloads and measures erasure encoding
and reconstruction throughput and latency.
Every sample verifies the reconstructed payload.
Use the report to compare compute backends and codec settings.
Storage and network performance require their own measurements.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " auto|cpu|cuda|hip|opencl"
Choose the requested compute backend.
The default is
.BR auto .
Unavailable GPU backends can fall back to CPU.
.TP
.BI \-\-scheme " reed-solomon|lrc|clay|msr|all"
Choose which erasure code to test.
The default is
.BR all .
.TP
.BI \-\-sizes " LIST"
Comma-separated payload sizes.
The default is
.BR 1MiB,8MiB,64MiB .
Accepted suffixes include B, KiB, MiB, GiB, K, M, and G.
.TP
.BI \-\-iterations " N"
Timed repetitions per size after warmup.
The default is 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-shards " N"
Override the scheme-specific data shard count.
.TP
.BI \-\-parity-shards " N"
Override the scheme-specific parity shard count.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpu-threshold-bytes " N"
Minimum payload size for GPU dispatch.
The default is 1048576.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Set the reproducible payload seed.
The default is 1262569289.
.TP
.BI \-\-json " FILE"
Write detailed timing, backend counters, and environment data as JSON in
addition to the console table.
.TP
.B \-\-require-acceleration
Fail unless GPU work executes without fallback.
An explicit GPU backend must also match the selected device backend.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the Kagi version.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
kagi-bench \-\-backend cpu \-\-scheme clay \-\-sizes 1MiB,8MiB \e
    \-\-json benchmark.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-build (1),
.BR test-all (1)
